    "material_a": "Labdanum Resinoid",
    "material_b": "Vanillin",
    "type": "synergy",
    "effect": "Classic amber accord cornerstone. Labdanum (VP~0.02 Pa, leathery-amber resinoid) and Vanillin (VP~0.002 Pa, creamy-sweet) form the amber triad when combined with benzoin. Labdanum's animalic-leather warmth is amplified and sweetened by vanillin's phenolic creaminess — the combination produces a sweetness greater than the sum of its parts via vanillin's suppression of labdanum's bitter facets. Documented in DB as one of three core pairings for labdanum.",
