    "axis": "depth"
  },
  {
    "material_a": "Labdanum Resinoid",
    "material_b": "Ethyl Vanillin",
    "type": "synergy",
    "effect": "More powerful variant of the labdanum+vanillin amber accord. Ethyl vanillin (3x stronger than vanillin, ODT ~0.02 ppb) intensifies the amber effect and adds a brighter, more confectionery edge. The increased potency means less material is needed, preserving labdanum's subtle leathery character while achieving the same sweet-amber effect. Ideal for modern amber bases where vanilla intensity is desired without the full dose of natural resinoid bulk.",
    "source": "agent-musk-fixative_2026-05-21",
    "axis": "depth"
  },
  {
    "material_a": "Labdanum Resinoid",
    "material_b": "Coumarin",
    "type": "pairing",
    "effect": "Labdanum's leathery-amber warmth + Coumarin's sweet hay-tonka = tobacco-amber accord reminiscent of pipe tobacco and vintage masculine elegance. Coumarin's dry-sweet hay character tempers labdanum's animalic edge while labdanum's warm leather provides a substantive foundation. This pairing bridges the amber and fougere families — found in compositions like Dior Homme Parfum where the amber-tobacco base underpins iris.",
    "source": "agent-musk-fixative_2026-05-21",
    "axis": "texture"
  },
  {
    "material_a": "Siam Benzoin",
    "material_b": "Coumarin",
    "type": "synergy",
    "effect": "Siam Benzoin's vanilla-almond balsamic warmth + Coumarin's hay-like sweet powder = amplified powdery-oriental accord. Together they produce a rich, almond-vanilla-tonka profile with a powdery texture far exceeding either alone. This is the essential 'powdery oriental' base — benzoin provides body and the vanilla-almond character; coumarin provides diffusivity and the hay-sweet top. Critical for DHI-style compositions where the powdery benzoin-coumarin accord bridges iris powderiness to deep amber.",
    "source": "agent-musk-fixative_2026-05-21",
    "axis": "texture"
  },
  {
    "material_a": "Musk Ketone",
    "material_b": "Ambrettolide",
    "type": "pairing",
    "effect": "Musk Ketone (nitro musk, VP~0.0003 Pa, powdery-animalic) + Ambrettolide (macrocyclic, VP~0.005 Pa, fruity-ambrette) = vintage-modern musk bridge. Musk Ketone provides a dense, powdery, slightly animalic old-guard warmth; Ambrettolide adds a naturalistic fruity-ambrette seed freshness and diffusion. Together they create a musk chord with vintage soul and modern radiance — the nitro musk anchors while the macrocyclic projects. Both are base-tier but Ambrettolide's slightly higher VP lifts Musk Ketone's density.",
    "source": "agent-musk-fixative_2026-05-21",
    "axis": "depth"
  },
  {
    "material_a": "Musk Ketone",
    "material_b": "Ethylene Brassylate",
    "type": "pairing",
    "effect": "Musk Ketone (nitro, powdery-animalic, MW 294) + Ethylene Brassylate (macrocyclic diester, lactonic-creamy, MW 418) = powdery-creamy musk chord. Musk Ketone provides the classic powder-sweet animalic depth reminiscent of vintage perfumery; Ethylene Brassylate's creamy lactonic character rounds and smooths it. The high molecular weight of both ensures exceptional longevity — this is the musk chord for compositions demanding 12h+ skin presence with a classic powder signature.",
    "source": "agent-musk-fixative_2026-05-21",
    "axis": "depth"
  },
  {
    "material_a": "Tonalide",
    "material_b": "Coumarin",
    "type": "pairing",
    "effect": "Tonalide (polycyclic, sweet-powdery musk, VP~0.005 Pa) + Coumarin (hay-sweet, VP~0.03 Pa) = unified sweet-musk base with warm powderiness. Tonalide's inherent sweetness and clean powder profile amplify coumarin's hay character while coumarin's slightly higher VP adds lift. Together they create a diffusive, warm, sweet base that sits between musk and tonka — ideal for the DHI heart where powdery iris meets sweet coumarin-musk warmth.",
    "source": "agent-musk-fixative_2026-05-21",
    "axis": "depth"
  },
  {
    "material_a": "Habanolide",
    "material_b": "Coumarin",
    "type": "pairing",
    "effect": "Habanolide (warm, ambery, slightly metallic macrocyclic musk) + Coumarin (sweet hay-tonka) = warm amber-musk base with tobacco sweetness. Habanolide's ambery warmth wraps around coumarin's sweet hay, creating a diffusive cloud with the comfort of amber and the nobility of tonka. This pairing is a gentler, more modern alternative to the classic coumarin + nitromusk combination — warmer, more transparent, and IFRA-compliant at all dose levels.",
    "source": "agent-musk-fixative_2026-05-21",
    "axis": "depth"
  },
  {
    "material_a": "Romandolide",
    "material_b": "Coumarin",
    "type": "pairing",
    "effect": "Romandolide (diffusive alicyclic musk, fruity-clean) + Coumarin (sweet hay-tonka) = radiant sweet base with musky lift. Romandolide's superior diffusivity (higher VP than standard macrocyclics) carries coumarin's sweetness outward, preventing it from sitting flatly on skin. Coumarin in turn gives Romandolide's clean-fruity profile a warm, noble body. Together they achieve the sweet, diffusive, slightly fruity-tonka musk character essential for contemporary niche compositions.",
    "source": "agent-musk-fixative_2026-05-21",
    "axis": "depth"
  },
  {
    "material_a": "Exaltolide",
    "material_b": "Vanillin",
    "type": "synergy",
    "effect": "Exaltolide (15-pentadecanolide, warm creamy-animalic macrocycle) + Vanillin (creamy-vanilla) = amplified creamy-sweet skin accord. Exaltolide's slightly animalic warmth and vanillin's creamy sweetness converge on skin to create the smell of skin itself — warm, slightly sweet, lived-in but clean. The synergy is in the shared 'creamy' axis: Exaltolide's macrocyclic lactone and vanillin's phenolic cream both contribute to a unified skin-cream effect that neither achieves alone.",
    "source": "agent-musk-fixative_2026-05-21",
    "axis": "skin_performance"
  },
  {
    "material_a": "Ethylene Brassylate",
    "material_b": "Coumarin",
    "type": "synergy",
    "effect": "Ethylene Brassylate's lactonic-creamy musk (macrocyclic diester) + Coumarin's sweet hay = creamy-tonka accord with exceptional longevity. EB's lactone ring provides a fatty-creamy mouthfeel that integrates coumarin's sweet dryness into a smoother, richer whole. The combined molecular weight (EB MW 418 + Coumarin MW 146) creates a dense, long-lived base — the EB carries the coumarin forward while the coumarin prevents EB from being purely creamy-blank.",
    "source": "agent-musk-fixative_2026-05-21",
    "axis": "depth"
  },
  {
    "material_a": "Habanolide",
    "material_b": "Vanillin",
    "type": "pairing",
    "effect": "Habanolide (warm ambery macrocyclic musk, slightly metallic) + Vanillin (creamy-vanilla sweetness) = warm amber-musk-vanilla base. Habanolide's ambery warmth and subtle metallic edge add sophistication to vanillin — preventing it from becoming straightforwardly foody or gourmand. The vanillin sweetens and softens Habanolide's metallic quality. Together they create a refined, warm, slightly radiant sweet-musk base suitable for the drydown of iris-amber compositions.",
    "source": "agent-musk-fixative_2026-05-21",
    "axis": "depth"
  },
  {
    "material_a": "Romandolide",
    "material_b": "Vanillin",
    "type": "pairing",
    "effect": "Romandolide (diffusive fruity-clean musk) + Vanillin (creamy vanilla) = radiant gourmand-musk with superior projection. Romandolide's inherently diffusive character lifts vanillin's heavy sweetness off the skin — the vanilla becomes airborne rather than sitting flat. Vanillin rounds Romandolide's potentially synthetic-clean edge with warmth. Together they create a modern gourmand-musk effect: vanilla that projects, musk that feels sweet and natural.",
    "source": "agent-musk-fixative_2026-05-21",
    "axis": "depth"
