    "material_a": "BHT",
    "material_b": "Vanillin",
    "type": "pairing",
    "effect": "BHT (butylated hydroxytoluene, antioxidant stabilizer, MW 220, VP~0.001 Pa) protects Vanillin from oxidative discoloration and degradation over time. Vanillin readily oxidizes to vanillic acid which causes browning, especially in ethanol solution exposed to light/air. BHT at 0.02–0.05% of concentrate scavenges free radicals and preserves vanilla's bright white-powder character. This is a functional pairing — BHT has negligible odor impact but substantially extends the shelf-stability of vanilla-containing formulations.",
    "source": "agent-musk-fixative_2026-05-21",
    "axis": "longevity"
